[Applause]  good evening ladies and gentlemen  friends and colleagues  welcome to the scientific and technical  Awards before we begin I'd like to take  a moment to acknowledge the entire  scientific and technical awards  committee  it's subcommittees and all the  surrogates who research and recommend  these awards these are men and women  from around the world who represent a  diverse spectrum of technical and  filmmaking skills including  cinematography digital imaging sound  production theatrical projection film  and laboratory processes lighting and  stage equipment mechanical or optical  effects virtual production  pre-visualization and editing we are  fortunate to have their dedication and  service which is entirely voluntary  this year the committee's initial review  totaled 72 submissions launching  investigations into 11 separate areas of  technology the amount of work that goes  into this process is astounding and the  fact that our volunteers take time out  of their busy lives is a testament to  their passion towards the advancement of  the art and science of motion pictures  many of these committee participants  have traveled a long way to join us here  tonight could those members of the main  committee the subcommittee's and all the  surrogates and all who participated in  the research and reports please stand  thank you  [Music]  we all thank you for the hundreds of  hours spent this year getting to this  evening tonight is part of the Academy's  celebration of 90 years of the Oscars so  we're adding something special this  evening as you are probably aware  tonight's award recipients are wearing  red boutonnieres  in addition previously awarded Gordon E  Sawyer and Oscar recipients and John a  Bonner metella commendation honorees are  wearing a white boutonniere these are  the elder statesmen of motion picture  science and our honored guests this  evening gentlemen would you please stand  [Applause]  the Academy's scientific and technical  awards are unique and that they cover  accomplishments that may take a decade  or more of invention refinement  engineering and evolution this evening  is an event that is special in the  industry it is a way for us to  acknowledge the deep appreciation and  respect that we have for the significant  technical contributions to our industry  I know that for some of you the  recognition being bestowed tonight is  honoring the culmination of a lifetime  of effort it has been a privilege to  chair this year's investigations and I  want to extend my congratulations to  everyone being honored here tonight the  show will start soon so sit back and  enjoy the evening thank you very much  [Applause]

